      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "That won't work the way you wish. Unity packages assets in different formats. One format is Windows/Mac/Linux which the PC version of VRChat uses. There's also Android which the quest version uses.\nTo be able to supply a PS4 version of VRChat with content, you'll need to generate PS4 assets with unity. Unity can in fact do this - you however need to have the PlayStation SDK to do so which you will only be able to get if you have an official developer license by Sony. So while the VRChat team might be able to supply you with some worlds or avatars. 99% of the user generated content won't be available which would limit such a version even more than the quest version.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
